From 1e9bec3c9cf9f5524bc07a7735b11df29fb73251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homeless3d <5290301+homeless3d@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:00:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Build against system Qt 6.11.2 (PySide6 6.11.2, GCC 16)
 and run natively on Wayland

Build system (BUILD_NOTES items 1, 2, 5-8):
- cmake/defaults/CY2026.cmake: PySide6 6.8.3 -> 6.11.2 (+ MD5 of the
  download.qt.io zip)
- RvCommon/CMakeLists.txt: find the Qt6 component GuiPrivate (the
  versionless Qt::GuiPrivate target is not defined on the system Qt)
- qt6.cmake: do not stage Qt's cmake/pkgconfig lib dirs (they clash with
  other dependency installs into stage/app/lib)
- python3.cmake: add numpy to RV_PYTHON_WHEEL_SAFE (numpy 2.3 from source
  fails: highway uses the evex512 target attribute GCC 16 dropped)
- make_pyside6.py: optional system libclang (RV_PYSIDE_SYSTEM_LLVM_DIR)
  instead of the 700 MB libclang download; PySide6 >= 6.9 source layout
- test_python_distribution.py: tkinter/sqlite3 imports are optional

Wayland runtime (BUILD_NOTES items 3, 4):
- RvDocument: only query the NV-GLX X11 extension when running on X11
  (QX11Info::display() is null on Wayland and crashed)
- GLView, rv/main.cpp: on Wayland request desktop OpenGL 4.1 compatibility
  and pin the default QSurfaceFormat, otherwise the shared EGL context
  becomes OpenGL ES 3.2 once QtWebEngine is loaded

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
